{"id":"river","name":"River","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:river"],"groups":["Figurative"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"River","text":"(1.) Heb. ‘aphik, properly the channel or ravine that holds water (2 Sam. 22:16), translated “brook,” “river,” “stream,” but not necessarily a perennial stream (Ezek. 6:3; 31:12; 32:6; 34:13). (2.) Heb. nahal, in winter a “torrent,” in summer a “wady” or valley (Gen. 32:23; Deut. 2:24; 3:16; Isa. 30:28; Lam. 2:18; Ezek. 47:9). These winter torrents sometimes come down with great suddenness and with desolating force. A distinguished traveller thus describes his experience in this matter:, “I was encamped in Wady Feiran, near the base of Jebel Serbal, when a tremendous thunderstorm burst upon us. After little more than an hour’s rain, the water rose so rapidly in the previously dry wady that I had to run for my life, and with great difficulty succeeded in saving my tent and goods; my boots, which I had not time to pick up, were washed away. In less than two hours a dry desert wady upwards …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5158","lemma":"נַחַל","xlit":"nachal","gloss":"a stream, especially a winter torrent","kjv":"brook, flood, river, stream","count":6,"share":0.32},{"strong":"H6388","lemma":"פֶּלֶג","xlit":"peleg","gloss":"a rill","kjv":"river, stream","count":4,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H4058","lemma":"מָדַד","xlit":"mâdad","gloss":"to stretch","kjv":"measure, mete, stretch self","count":3,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H7495","lemma":"רָפָא","xlit":"râphâʼ","gloss":"to mend","kjv":"cure, heal, physician, repair","count":3,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H6921","lemma":"קָדִים","xlit":"qâdîym","gloss":"the fore or front part","kjv":"east","count":3,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H3381","lemma":"יָרַד","xlit":"yârad","gloss":"to descend","kjv":"abundantly, bring down, carry down, cast down","count":4,"share":0.21}],"verses":["Ps.36.8","Ezek.47.5","Ezek.47.6","Ezek.47.7","Ezek.47.9","Ezek.47.12","Ps.46.4","Ps.119.136","Isa.32.